course: dictionary
lesson: 11403
title: Accomplished: done well, or very skilled
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Accomplished can mean finished successfully. «The team accomplished their mission before lunch.» They finished the job and succeeded, so accomplished means done or achieved.
explain: Accomplished can also describe a person who is very skilful after lots of practice. «Maya is an accomplished pianist, and she practises every day.» The word tells you she is good at playing, and that she got good through practice.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like practice, skill, finished and succeeded point to accomplished. Try swapping in "skilful" or "finished" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Accomplished can be the past form of the verb accomplish: «She accomplished her goal.»
fact: Other forms of the verb are accomplish, accomplishes and accomplishing.
fact: As an adjective, accomplished means very skilful after much practice: «an accomplished reader».
fact: «Mission accomplished» means a task has been finished successfully.
fact: In formal writing, «an accomplished fact» means something that has already happened and cannot be undone.
exercise: «Ben finally accomplished his goal of reading one hundred books.» What does accomplished mean here? | Argued about | Forgot about | Gave up | *Finished successfully
exercise: «Aisha is an accomplished swimmer who has trained since she was five.» What does accomplished suggest? | Lost in the pool | Frightened of water | Lazy and bored | *Very skilful, after lots of practice
exercise: Which word is the past form of the verb accomplish? | accomplishes | accomplish | *accomplished | accomplishing
test: «The class accomplished the project in one week.» Which word means about the same as accomplished here? | *Achieved | Dropped | Repeated | Started
test: «Sam is an accomplished artist, and his paintings hang in galleries.» What does accomplished mean? | *Very skilful after much practice | Messy and careless | Unfinished | Hurried and rushed
exam: «The robot's mission was accomplished, and it sent back photos from Mars.» Which meaning fits best? | Not yet begun | *Successfully completed | Abandoned halfway | Hidden from view
